        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nathalie Sarraute, Anchee Min, Alain Robbe-Grillet, Michel Butor, Claude Simon\n- Roles: lawyer, writer, author\n- Topics: Nouveau Roman, new novel\n- Places: Shanghai, San Francisco\n\nFacts:\n- Nathalie Sarraute was born on July 18, 1900, and she was a French lawyer and writer.\n- Anchee Min, also known as Min Anqi, was born on January 14, 1957, in Shanghai, China.\n- Alain Robbe-Grillet was one of the figures most associated with the Nouveau Roman, or new novel, trend of the 1960s.\n- The 1960s Nouveau Roman trend was also associated with Nathalie Sarraute, Michel Butor, and Claude Simon.\n- Anchee Min is a Chinese-American author who lives in San Francisco and Shanghai.\n- Nathalie Sarraute died on October 19, 1999.",
